Z||000000||npavlo||09-14-2000||09:49 PM||||it seems to me more people are putting OHV 3.4s in there cars than 3.4L DOHCs.. why is that?  i know you keep the stock apperacance.. is that it?  i guess thats cool.. since i have an extra 3.4L DOHC plus the one in my cutlass.. i think ill be going the DOHC way.. =).. is this bad?  <P>------------------<BR>1991 Cutlass Supreme International 3.4L DOHC<BR>5-Speed Getrag 284<BR>Blown Trans, possibly going into fiero --||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||09-14-2000||10:07 PM||||DOHC's are more work to install.||||reg||1
Z||000002||3400Fiero||09-15-2000||02:36 PM||||I have 3400 DOHC from a Monte Carlo in my Fiero, and love it!  I think it may be more work only because you will probably have to make a custom exhaust (I have a dual exhaust with H-pipe over the trans) and may have to modify the passenger's side lid hinge and strut tower brace to get it to fit right, and obviously modify the wiring. It is definitely worth it!  If you have any questions, I would be happy to help.  I did my conversion without a kit, and I don't think a kit is really worth the $1800 you'd have to spend (unless you don't feel comfortable modifying the wiring).<P>------------------<BR>1988 Fiero 3400DOHC<BR>||||reg||14
